# Harmony Patches

## Prefer

```csharp
[HarmonyPatch(typeof(SomeType), nameof(SomeType.SomeMethod))]
public static class SomeType_SomeMethod_Patch
{
    public static void Postfix(/* ... */) { /* additive change */ }
}
```

- Prefer `Postfix` or `Prefix` (bool skip) over `Transpiler`.
- Target with `typeof` + `nameof`. Avoid bare string method names unless overload forces it.
- One concern per patch class; name as `TypeName_MethodName_Patch`.

## Avoid

- Broad reflective scans or silent catch-all `try/catch` that hide patch failures.
- Transpilers unless Postfix/Prefix cannot achieve the goal — then comment why and keep IL edits minimal.
- Patching before required game systems exist without an explicit deferred hook.

## Safety

- Assume other mods patch the same method; keep changes additive when possible.
- If a Prefix skips the original, document the condition and user-visible impact.
